3:["$","main",null,{"id":"main-content","className":"min-h-screen bg-bg pt-24","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-14","children":[["$","$L10",null,{"href":"/learning-centre","className":"text-sm font-semibold text-accent hover:text-fg transition-colors","children":"Back to Learning Centre"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-8 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8 md:p-10","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent","children":"Google Ads Leaks · Clicks Without Conversions"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-fg md:text-5xl","children":"Fix Google Ads Landing Pages to Transform Clicks Into Sales"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"If Google Ads is producing clicks but no sales, the campaign may be doing exactly what it should: creating arrival. The chain breaks when the landing page does not continue the conversation the ad started. Raising budget or adjusting bidding strategy does not fix what happens after the click."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-stretch sm:items-center gap-3","children":[["$","$L10",null,{"href":"/audit?utm_source=learning-centre-google-ads-clicks-no-sales&utm_medium=hero-cta","className":"inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center justify-center rounded bg-accent px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-bg transition-opacity hover:opacity-85","children":"Get your free audit →"}],["$","$L10",null,{"href":"/repair-sprint","className":"inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center justify-center rounded border border-border px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-fg-muted transition-colors hover:border-fg-muted hover:text-fg","children":"Explore $97 Repair Sprint"}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"data-editorial":"answer-first","className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Direct answer: isolate the post-click leak before changing budget"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"A Google Ads click represents a visitor who searched for something specific and decided your ad was relevant enough to click. First verify the search term, ad promise, and conversion tracking. Then compare page behaviour by campaign, device, and landing page. A click with no sale narrows the investigation; it does not identify the cause by itself."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"If relevant clicks reach a correctly tracked page but visitors disengage before the offer or form, investigate message match, mobile load, proof, and CTA friction before buying more traffic. Change one suspected cause and measure it against the baseline."}],["$","aside",null,{"role":"note","aria-label":"Evidence boundary","className":"mt-5 rounded-xl border border-border px-5 py-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-fg","children":"Evidence boundary:"}]," CTR, bounce, and conversion events can support a page-side hypothesis, but they do not prove causality or exclude targeting, offer, tracking, and auction effects. No diagnosis or page change guarantees a sales outcome."]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-5 flex flex-col gap-2 text-sm","children":[["$","$L10",null,{"href":"/learning-centre/message-match-checklist","className":"font-semibold text-accent hover:text-fg","children":"Compare search intent with page messaging"}],["$","$L10",null,{"href":"/learning-centre/landing-page-not-converting","className":"font-semibold text-accent hover:text-fg","children":"Diagnose five common landing-page leaks"}]]}]]}],"$L11","$L12","$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16"]}]}]
